{"name":"Oyster Bay","hex":"#71818c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Oyster Bay","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A town, hamlet, and census-designated place therein, in Nassau County, Long Island, New York, United States. \nAn inlet in Nassau County, New York.","An inlet in Nassau County, New York."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Oyster_Bay"}],"entries":[{"title":"Oyster Bay, New South Wales","blocks":[{"text":"Oyster Bay is a suburb in Southern Sydney, in the state of New South Wales, Australia. It is located 26 kilometres south of the Sydney central business district in the local government area of the Sutherland Shire."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Oyster_Bay.jpg/330px-Oyster_Bay.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oyster_Bay%2C_New_South_Wales","wikidata":"Q3643583"},{"title":"Great Oyster Bay","blocks":[{"text":"Great Oyster Bay is a broad and sheltered bay on the east coast of Tasmania, Australia which opens onto the Tasman Sea. The Tasman Highway runs close to the West Coast of the bay with views of the granite peaks of the Hazards and Schouten Island of the Freycinet Peninsula which are incorporated in the Freycinet National Park."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Freycinet_Peninsula_NASA.jpg/330px-Freycinet_Peninsula_NASA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_Oyster_Bay","wikidata":"Q4148428"},{"title":"Oyster","blocks":[{"text":"Oyster is the common name for a number of different families of salt-water bivalve molluscs that live in marine or brackish habitats. In some species, the valves are highly calcified, and many are somewhat irregular in shape. Many oysters are in the superfamily Ostreoidea."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Crassostrea_gigas_p1040848.jpg/330px-Crassostrea_gigas_p1040848.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oyster","wikidata":"Q107411"},{"title":"Bay","blocks":[{"text":"A bay is a recessed, coastal body of water that directly connects to a larger main body of water, such as an ocean, a lake, or another bay. A large bay is usually called a gulf, sea, sound, or bight. A cove is a small, circular bay with a narrow entrance. A fjord is an elongated bay formed by glacial action.\nThe term embayment is also used for related features, such as extinct bays or freshwater environments."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Aerial_photograph_of_Langness_and_the_bay_at_Castletown_13_February_2014_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3847162.jpg/330px-Aerial_photograph_of_Langness_and_the_bay_at_Castletown_13_February_2014_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3847162.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bay","wikidata":"Q39594"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Oyster_Bay_shops.jpg/500px-Oyster_Bay_shops.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Oyster_Bay_shops.jpg/500px-Oyster_Bay_shops.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Oyster Bay Road and Como Road intersection","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOyster_Bay_shops.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Blick_ueber_Great_Oyster_Bay_zur_Freycinet_Peninsula.jpg/500px-Blick_ueber_Great_Oyster_Bay_zur_Freycinet_Peninsula.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Blick_ueber_Great_Oyster_Bay_zur_Freycinet_Peninsula.jpg/500px-Blick_ueber_Great_Oyster_Bay_zur_Freycinet_Pe